Pumpkin Bread
  --Molly Baz

nonstick vegetable oil spray
2 1/2 c ap flour
2 tsp cinnamon
2 tsp kosher salt
1 tsp baking powder
1/2 tsp baking soda
1/2 tsp freshly grated nutmeg
1/8 tsp ground cloves
2 large eggs
15 oz can pumpkin puree
1 tbsp + 1 tsp finely grated ginger (3" nub)
1 1/2 c + 1 tbsp sugar
1 c evoo
1/2 c raw pumpkin seeds

Preheat oven to 235F. Lightly coat 9x5" loaf pan with nonstick spray; line bottom with parchment paper, leaving generous overhang (sling) on both sides. Whisk flour, cinnamon, salt, baking powder, baking soda, nutmeg, and cloves in a medium bowl. Whisk eggs, pumpkin puree, ginger, and 1 1/2 c sugar in large bowl. Stream in oil, whisking constantly until mixture is homogenous. Gently fold half the dry ingredients into egg mixture until no dry spots remain. Repeat with remaining dry ingredients, stirring to combine but be careful not to overmix. Transfer batter to prepared pan; smooth top with a spatula. Scatter pumpkin seeds over batter, pressing lightly to adhere. Sprinkle seeds with remaining 1 tbsp sugar. Bake bread, rotating pan halfway through, until a tester inserted into the center comes out clean, 80-90 min. Let cool slightly, then run a knife or small offset spatula around pan to help loosen bread. Using sling, transfer bread to a wire rack and let cool. Bread can be baked 4 days ahear. Cover tightly with plastic wrap and keep at room temp.



Alt version:
  --Billie Eilish & Maggie

1 3/4 c (15 oz can/408 g) pumpkin puree
1 c (209g) light brown sugar
1/4 c (57g) sugar
2 tsp pumpkin pie spice
1/2 tsp ground ginger
1/2 tsp nutmeg (freshly ground if possible)
1 tsp cinnamon
1/4 tsp ground cloves
2/3 c vegetable oil
1 1/2 tsp vanilla bean paste
2 c (250 g) ap flour or 284 g 1 to 1 GF flour
1/2 tsp salt
1 tsp baking soda
3/4 tsp baking powder
Walnuts or pecans (optional) up to 1 c chopped
raisins (optional)

Preheat the oven to 350F. Grease either a 9″  loaf pan or 4 small loaf pans with plant based butter or oil. In a bowl or x-large glass measuring cup, combine and whisk together pumpkin puree, light brown sugar, sugar, salt, vegetable oil and vanilla bean paste. Once well blended, add pumpkin pie spice, ginger, nutmeg, cinnamon, cloves, baking powder and baking soda and stir to combine. Gently stir in the flour until the mixture it is mostly combined but there might still be some clumps. It won’t be entirely smooth but it is important not to overmix. If adding nuts or raisins, carefully and gently add them at this point (or you can place half of the batter in your pan on one end and add nuts or raisins to the other half). Pour the batter into the prepared pan and place into your preheated oven for ~1 hr (considerably less  30-40 min if using smaller pans). Keep an eye on the center of the bread to make sure it is set before removing from the oven. A toothpick inserted should come out clean. Remove bread to a wire rack and allow to cool for 10 min before inverting and removing from pan. Allow to cool further on the rack.


Note: if you don't have pumpkin spice or individual spices, can double the one you have
